     Searching 32 times does not guarantee that you'd find something
hidden (although chances are extremely high that you would).  What
probably happened was that there was a hidden corridor branching off
a corridor somewhere other than the "dead ends" that you searched.

     You could have avoided starvation by waiting until you were weak
from hunger and then #pray.  This won't work 100% of the time, but it
usually will.  In your case, if the were patient enough, defeating
randomly created monsters would have given you a chance to increase in
level, and once high enough some of the them would have been rock-diggers
or leave behind useful scrolls and/or wands.  So even without searching,
you might have been able to get away from your current predicament.
(I doubt if many players are patient enough to bother attempting that. :-)
Besides searching the walls, you could search the room interiors for
trap doors ands teleport traps.  Another alternative would be to find a
trap door on the level above and keep going back up and jumping through
it until you landed in either the unreached area or a lower level.  Once
in the unreached area, the connection to the explored area likely would
have become evident.



